    "noAmmunition": [
      "Hpt_BeamLaser_Fixed_Small",
      "Hpt_PulseLaser_Gimbal_Medium",
      "Hpt_MiningLaser_Fixed_Small",
      "Int_DroneControl_Collection_Size3_Class3"
    ],
    "journalReadings": {
      "note": "Every non-zero AmmoInClip / AmmoInHopper across the nineteen journal captures — the only external readings of what a module had *loaded* that this repository holds. They are not the only external check on `clipSize` and `ammoMaximum`: the `AmmoClipSize` and `AmmoMaximum` modifiers a capture states on an engineered module are a second and stronger one, joined by `fixtures/ships/module-stats.jsonc` `capturedBaseStats`, and in-game verification does not reach a *hardpoint's* reserve ammo. All ninety-two sit exactly at capacity, on twenty-six distinct modules, several of which appear in more than one capture. A reading is still only a lower bound on what a module holds and must never be read straight back as a catalogue figure: a journal's ammunition is the ship's rearm state at the instant of capture, so a partly spent launcher would report less than its capacity and say nothing about the catalogue. What does settle a capacity is the `AmmoMaximum` modifier a capture states on an engineered module, which gives the base and the engineered figure together — the Lynx Highliner's heat-sink launcher reports 3 in reserve under a grade-1 Heat Sink Capacity against a base of 2, so the reading alone would have been the engineered value. Spire Ops and Slapaconda add three Caustic Sink launcher readings at 1/7 and six pre-engineered Heat Sink launcher readings at 1/4, all with their base and fitted reserves stated. On the Corsair the capacity is likewise the engineered one, since three of its five ammunition-bearing weapons carry an `AmmoClipSize` or `AmmoMaximum` modifier; the two plasma accelerators take Long Range, which charges neither. The Corvette's large gimballed cannon sits at capacity under a grade-5 Overcharged, which is Frontier's own reading that the recipe does not cut a cannon's clip — a 15% penalty would have loaded four rounds. The plasma Corvette's medium fragment cannon sits at its magazine of 3 under a grade-4 Overcharged, which is consistent with that group's absent clip leg without being evidence of it: a −12% cut leaves 3 × 0.88 = 2.64, which rounds back to 3, so there the modifier list is what says the leg is absent and the loaded count says nothing. The Caspian Explorer's medium plasma accelerator says the same again at grade 1, where the cut would be −3% and 5 × 0.97 = 4.85 rounds back to 5. That reading is evidence and not a guard: a build parsed from a journal folds the modifiers the journal states, so adding a clip leg to the recipe would not move these counts. What fails on such a change is the engineering suite, which folds the recipe itself.",
      "readings": 92,
      "distinctModules": 26,
      "atCapacity": 92,
      "belowCapacity": []
    },
    "engineered": {
      "note": "Every roll here is at full quality on an empty Viper, refitted per roll. An engineered clip is rounded up to a whole burst where the roll is computed; the reserve is rounded to the nearest whole round after every contribution is applied.",
