    "engineeredGroundTruth": {
      "note": "Every engineered clip or reserve Frontier states across the nineteen journal captures — thirty-seven readings on eleven of them. `game` is the modifier the journal states and what the weapon had loaded; `simulated` is what `computeModifiers` produces for the same recipe, grade and corrected quality, or what the fixed pre-engineered variant supplies when `preEngineered` is true; an imported build uses the stated modifier verbatim and therefore always equals `game`. Thirty-six agree exactly, including a fragment cannon's Corrosive Shell reserve at quality 0.826, where the leg is the experimental's flat −20% rather than a quality-rolled one, and the Spire Ops and Slapaconda Caustic Sink rolls and tech-broker Heat Sink variants. The two multi-cannon captures report stale fractional qualities even though the modules are fully engineered, so `reportedQuality` preserves the verbatim journal value while `quality` records the manually verified value used for simulation. Nearest-integer reserve rounding reproduces the Corsair's 87 rounds and the Lynx Highliners' and Panther's 3 heat sinks. The Corsair dumbfire rack is the deliberate exception: it was engineered under the legacy system, where attributes advanced independently, so its one reported `Quality` cannot reproduce both per-leg values through the current shared-quality model. `clipSize` is omitted from `game` and `simulated` where the recipe carries no clip leg and the magazine stands at its catalogue figure.",
